        </button>

        <div class="about-story-label">
          <svg width="25" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 3h12v18l-6-4-6 4z"/></svg>
          <span>What we believe</span>
        </div>

        <p class="about-belief">The best firms are not the ones with the most clients. They are the ones whose work travels without them. Do good work. Let God see.</p>
      </aside>

      <section class="about-copy-column">
        <p>In 2019, we took a diaper brand in Dubai that nobody had heard of. We did not start with ads. We started with free trials in Facebook mother groups. 400 leads. 60% conversion. The product sold before the brand existed.</p>
        <p>That taught us something most marketing firms never learn: <strong>growth does not start with campaigns. It starts with understanding who is already buying and why.</strong></p>
        <p>A few years later, a sneaker brand in the US came to us after crossing $1M in sales. They could not tell us who their buyer was. We stopped guessing and started asking. The answer changed everything. $500 in monitored sales became $3,000 a month in under 40 days. Not from more spend. From understanding.</p>
        <p>That is what Mediacup does. We find the insight that changes the economics, then we build the system that compounds it.</p>
        <p>We are not a large firm. That is intentional. Every engagement begins with a direct conversation with the Founding Partner. The person who diagnoses the problem is the same person who designs the solution. We operate embedded within the business, not advising from the outside. Close to the problem. Close to the team. Accountable to outcomes.</p>
        <p>We work across D2C, retail, real estate, education, and hospitality in India, the UK, the UAE, the USA, and Belgium. Our clients include Godrej, FabIndia, Hirandani, DY Patil, Fern Hotels, Best Western, and FCTRYLAB.</p>
